P-1 (spec 017, the night shift; plan.md §10; tasks.md T064): deploy/night-shift/ becomes human-only, and the night
shift's sign-in token is denied by name.

What it changes, in every layer the repository uses for a human-only path:
  - .claude/settings.json: permissions.deny gains Edit(/deploy/night-shift/**); sandbox.filesystem.denyWrite gains
    ./deploy/night-shift; sandbox.credentials.envVars gains CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, mode deny (FR-036; plan §13's
    first risk: where Claude Code's own sandbox runs, no command it starts can read the token).
  - .claude/hooks/protected-paths.sh: deploy/night-shift and everything under it is refused to every Edit, Write,
    MultiEdit, and NotebookEdit, by both path resolutions and in linked worktrees, like deploy/agents-engine.

Spec IDs: decision 4 ("Live copy stays outside, and we can have an example copy inside under a human-only path"),
FR-016 (the example copy at deploy/night-shift/containers/), FR-036, and the Assumptions' "Agent configuration outside
.claude/" deviation, which this patch and P-10 hold.

Needed for: the merge of feat/017-the-night-shift (plan.md §10). Apply it before P-5, whose matrix rows prove it.

How to apply, on your own branch, from the repository's root (one line each):
  B=feat/017-g5-patches
  F=docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-p1.patch
  git show "refs/heads/$B:$F" > /tmp/p1.patch
  sha256sum /tmp/p1.patch
  patch -p1 --dry-run < /tmp/p1.patch
  patch -p1 < /tmp/p1.patch
The SHA-256 to compare is in docs/merge-requests/2026-11-12-feat-017-patches.md.

Verified on a fresh `git archive refs/heads/main` export (main d4870ec8), never a worktree: patch -p1 --dry-run, then
patch -p1, both clean; `jq . .claude/settings.json` parses; `bash -n` and `shellcheck -x` on the hook are clean. With
P-5 and P-3 applied too, `bash redteam/forbidden-actions.sh` on that export: 1023 passed, 25 failed, 66 known gaps,
"every listed row ran". The 25 failures are stage S's, the same 25 the unpatched export fails (an export isn't the
sandboxed checkout, so its masks don't apply there); every new row passes, and the one new known gap is P-5's.

